Wed Nov 18 08:47:43 UTC 2026 - Alberto Planas Dominguez <aplanas@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.0+git20260324.41044ec:
  * Add warning on compatibility
  * CMake: enable dumb dongle option for core
  * Add dummy Init_Done callback for new canokey-core
  * doc: add CI badge in README
  * chore: fix review comments by Copilot
  * ci: add GitHub Actions build workflow
  * fix: update device_loop() call to match current canokey-core API
  * docs: remove outdated Mac mbedtls patching instructions
  * build: modernize CMakeLists.txt and update library paths
  * deps: update canokey-core to latest snapshot
- Drop mbedtls-fix-building-with-GCC-16.patch, mbedtls was replaced
  by TF-PSA-Crypto
- Refresh canokey-git.diff and canokey-core-static.diff
- Add BuildRequires python3, python3-Jinja2 and python3-jsonschema,
  needed to generate the CTAP GetInfo data and TF-PSA-Crypto code
- Add canokey-core-fm-return-type.patch, return an error from the
  NFC chip functions when no chip is selected (-Werror=return-type)
- Library soname is now libcanokey-qemu.so.1. FIDO2 credentials
  registered with the old version (resident and non-resident, e.g.
  systemd-cryptenroll slots) do not work with the new one and must
  be enrolled again
- Add the canokey-qemu-libvirt subpackage: a state directory
  /var/lib/libvirt/qemu/canokey, an AppArmor rule for it,
  and README.SUSE describing how to attach the key to a libvirt guest

